      "problem": "If $\\pi ,\\text{e}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$ are elements of $Y$, but $0$ and $1$ are not, then which of the following is true?",
      "worked_solution": "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since $\\pi ,\\text{e}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$ are elements of $Y,$ we write $\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\in Y.$\n\n- Since $0$ and $1$ are *not* elements of $Y,$ we write $0,1\\notin Y.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  $\\pi ,\\text{e},\\sqrt{2}\\in Y$ and $0,1\\notin Y$",
